Z||000000||88formula||04-22-2001||02:43 PM||||I'm looking for a header that takes advantage of wave dynamics or suction waves to help scavenge the exhaust gases out of the cylinder like a true header should. I know the sprint manifolds are not much better than stock ported manifolds. The Chris West units have been dynoed by 1FST2M6 and didn't make any real power gains over the stock manifolds. In fact he lost most of his low end torque, which shouldn’t happen if the header is a tuned header. I'm wondering if the FOCOA headers are any better.<P><BR>Thanks in advance guys.<BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
